course: dictionary
lesson: 805
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around them, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Begging» comes from the verb beg, which means asking for something very strongly, because you really want it or need it.
explain: Read this sentence: «Cuckoos lay their eggs in other birds' nests; the cuckoo chick pushes the other eggs out, and its loud begging, which sounds like a whole nest of hungry chicks, makes the foster parents feed a chick much bigger than themselves.» The chick is not asking people for money. The clues are hungry chicks and feed, so begging means loudly calling out for food.
explain: Always test your meaning. Swap it into the sentence: «its loud asking for food» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. If a meaning does not fit the clues, try a different one.
fact: Begging means asking someone very strongly or desperately for something.
fact: In the cuckoo sentence, «begging» means the chick's loud calls for food.
fact: Begging can also mean asking people in the street for money or food because you are poor.
fact: «Going begging» means not wanted or not taken, as in «there's a cake going begging».
fact: «I beg your pardon» is a polite way of saying sorry, or asking someone to repeat what they said.
exercise: «Cuckoos lay their eggs in other birds' nests... its loud begging... makes the foster parents feed a chick much bigger than themselves.» What does begging mean in this sentence? | Singing a happy song | *Loudly calling out for food | Building a new nest | Sitting quietly in the nest
exercise: There is a cake going begging on the table. What does this mean? | Someone is begging for it right now | It is a birthday cake | The cake is burnt | *Nobody has taken it
exercise: A man sits on the pavement with a begging bowl. What is he doing? | Playing music for fun | *Asking people for money because he is poor | Selling bowls in a shop | Cooking his dinner
test: The puppy sat up and begged for a biscuit. What does begged mean here? | Ran away from the kitchen | Barked at the postman | *Sat up and asked for food | Fell fast asleep
test: Mum said, «Please stop begging for one more game.» What does begging mean here? | Looking for a lost toy | Being very quiet | *Asking very strongly for something you really want | Asking people for money in the street
exam: Which sentence uses begging to mean asking people for money? | The child was begging for one more story. | *A man sat on the corner, begging for coins because he had no home. | The cake was going begging on the table. | The dog was begging for a biscuit.
